From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas <thomas.giudici@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 27 Apr 2026 14:23:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 22/23] pthread_create: always reserve a guard page above the
 thread stack

The secondary stack randomization patch replaced the previously fixed
one-page guard between the thread stack and the pthread_internal_t /
static TLS region with a randomly sized gap:

    size_t gap_size = __builtin_align_up(arc4random_uniform(max_gap_size),
                                         page_size());

arc4random_uniform(N) is uniform over [0, N) and can return 0.
__builtin_align_up(0, page_size()) is 0, so when that happens gap_size
becomes 0 and the subsequent mprotect() makes the writable non-stack
region directly abut the writable stack with no PROT_NONE guard page
between them. A linear stack overflow then silently corrupts
pthread_internal_t / static TLS instead of faulting.

The probability is 1/max_gap_size per pthread_create() call (about
1 / (stack_size/2 / page_size) on 64-bit), so it is rare but real and
defeats the invariant introduced by the earlier 'move pthread_internal_t
behind guard page' commit. The surrounding comment block still describes
'(random) guard page(s)' between stack and pthread_internal_t,
confirming this is unintended.

Clamp gap_size to at least one page so randomization is preserved while
the guard page is always present.
---
 libc/bionic/pthread_create.cpp | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libc/bionic/pthread_create.cpp b/libc/bionic/pthread_create.cpp
index 72cff2e..aa793f7 100644
--- a/libc/bionic/pthread_create.cpp
+++ b/libc/bionic/pthread_create.cpp
@@ -237,8 +237,13 @@ ThreadMapping __allocate_thread_mapping(size_t stack_size, size_t stack_guard_si
 #else
   size_t max_gap_size = stack_size / 10;
 #endif
-  // Make sure random stack top guard size are multiples of page size.
+  // Make sure the random stack top guard size is a multiple of the page size,
+  // and always reserve at least one guard page between the stack and the
+  // pthread_internal_t / static TLS region. arc4random_uniform() can return 0,
+  // and align_up(0, page_size) is 0, which would leave no guard page at all
+  // and let a stack overflow silently corrupt pthread_internal_t.
   size_t gap_size = __builtin_align_up(arc4random_uniform(max_gap_size), page_size());
+  if (gap_size == 0) gap_size = page_size();
 
   // Allocate in order: stack guard, stack, (random) guard page(s), pthread_internal_t, static TLS, libgen buffers, guard page.
   size_t mmap_size;
